{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat collab/yang-clojure/1794700000000-engineer-d1-r9b-corpus-rebuild.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md collab/yang-clojure/1794671000001-d1-bounds-declaration-draft.md collab/yang-clojure/1794390804000-cc3-bounded-run-declaration-v2.md'","aggregated_output":"# D1 r9b Jupiter: corpus rebuild started, incomplete\n\nThis updates `1794698000000-engineer-d1-r9-jupiter.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md` by reference. **Partial only: 8 of 155 fixtures passed the static gate; 147 remain not run.** No Jupiter bounds declaration, tagged run, D1 corpus record, verification result, or companion has been completed. No commit; the retention-location owner decision remains pending.\n\nThe batch pass outcome now retains the six actual segment addresses returned by persistence: input, snapshot, evidence, profile, root and stamped-root. The batch record refuses a pass missing any of these addresses. A storage delta of zero is permitted because deduplicated replay can add no bytes. The record remains bookkeeping, not a verification result. Each admission is generated by the existing fresh run and recorded with its origin; no historical coordinates are invented.\n\nScratch progress is `target/d1-r9b-outcomes.edn` (SHA-256 at this stopping point `cfffefb46cebc49c74a44b6db739d32bb5e8bd631d3b382d9d9b6faf773f1f3b`), with its store at `target/d1-r9b-store/content.jing` (26,292,420 bytes). These are local scratch, not published retention. The first process was interrupted after seven recorded passes; a fresh process reopened the store and progress file and added one pass. A separate fresh process then reopened the store, fetched all 48 addresses for the eight passes, and checked that each input and snapshot origin equalled the recorded admission origin. This demonstrates process-interruption resume for this sample, not a power-loss test or the completed corpus.\n\nRed first: an outcome missing addresses was accepted before the change and refused afterward; a zero-byte pass was refused before the change and accepted afterward. The focused batch test passes 1 test / 9 assertions. Before the zero-byte adjustment the standing battery passed 57 tests / 702 assertions; the focused test covers the subsequent adjustment. The restarted corpus invocation passed 1 test / 9 assertions. clj-kondo reports 0 errors and 0 warnings on the three changed files. The frozen `slice9_site_tables.edn` SHA-256 remains `e435ac4072ba0a3c278fbe91918d22184b43f0a8d6c1e397c09f68dd629beb75`. No full oracle suite or tagged lane was run.\n\nTo resume, keep both scratch paths together, set `target/d1-corpus-run.edn` to their paths and the desired `:D1_CORPUS_BATCH`, then run `clojure -M:test -n yang.latte-oracle-test -v yang.latte-oracle-test/test-d1-corpus-static-gates` with the configured JVM environment. Outcomes are final, and the progress file identifies the remaining fixtures. After the full rebuild, measure actual Jupiter lane, heap, size and phase maxima before declaring ceilings; do not borrow laptop bounds. The r9 limitations on verifier completeness and provenance remain unresolved and must be resolved before any verification-result claim.\n\n## Continuation on 2026-11-16\n\nThe existing run resumed with a 25-fixture batch, using the same outcomes file and store, with spot checks enabled. The invocation completed successfully (1 test, 9 assertions, 0 failures/errors); all 25 new outcomes passed. A separate process reopened the store and fetched all six retained addresses for each of the 33 passes, and checked that each fetched input and snapshot origin matched its recorded admission origin. Its summary was **155 fixtures: 33 pass, 0 refused, 122 not run; 198 addresses checked**. This is still a partial static corpus rebuild, not a verification result.\n\nAt this stopping point `target/d1-r9b-outcomes.edn` SHA-256 is `ea2b6829d6a33a5bfe32e312dc6b93e91e4181e633b9c46de45471e2227264a8`; `target/d1-r9b-store/content.jing` is 154,053,237 bytes. The batch log is `target/d1-r9b-batch-2.log` and the reopen check is `target/d1-r9b-check-2.log`. The check was run using `java -cp \"$(clojure -Spath -A:test)\" clojure.main target/d1-r9b-check.clj`; two preliminary attempts accidentally invoked the test alias's broad default suite and were interrupted, so they are not completed test results. The frozen table SHA-256 remains `e435ac4072ba0a3c278fbe91918d22184b43f0a8d6c1e397c09f68dd629beb75`.\n\nNo code was changed in this continuation. No Jupiter bounds declaration, tagged lane, corpus correspondence record, verification result, or companion has been completed. No commit was made. Preserve both scratch paths together; the configured next batch remains 25 fixtures. The previous red-first and kondo results above describe the preexisting changes, not new tests from this continuation. The r9 verifier and provenance limitations remain open.\n\n## Continuation: third batch on 2026-11-16\n\nThe next 25 fixtures passed the static gates (1 test, 9 assertions, 0 failures/errors; `target/d1-r9b-batch-3.log`). A fresh process reopened the shared store, fetched all six retained addresses for each pass, and checked that the input and snapshot origins matched the recorded admissions (`target/d1-r9b-check-3.log`): **155 fixtures, 58 pass, 0 refused, 97 not run; 348 addresses checked**. This remains a partial static rebuild, not a verification result. The progress file SHA-256 at that checkpoint was `802386972c1e8fbd128511e9be18a3bfe6d2593aa6a97e143f02e8d9c46b9b48`; the store was 461,259,401 bytes. The frozen table SHA-256 was still `e435ac4072ba0a3c278fbe91918d22184b43f0a8d6c1e397c09f68dd629beb75`. No code changed in this continuation and no commit was made. The undeclared bounds, verifier limitations, and missing tagged run and publications described above remain open.\n\nThe fourth batch then completed with 25 more passes (1 test, 9 assertions, 0 failures/errors; `target/d1-r9b-batch-4.log`), reaching 83 pass and 72 not run. At this checkpoint the outcomes SHA-256 was `89be38012ead5dcd16d9ca6c9316c4c01f0d7665fb0759e817d791b166138c02` and the store was 560,561,698 bytes. The independent reopen check above covers the preceding 58 passes; it has not yet been repeated for this checkpoint.\n\nThe fifth batch completed with 25 more passes (1 test, 9 assertions, 0 failures/errors; `target/d1-r9b-batch-5.log`): 108 pass and 47 not run. The outcomes SHA-256 at that checkpoint was `b2b69880cf0a3567ed022be644f50d4bc2c892323d107103baf4b89719028ead`; store size was 628,794,487 bytes. The separate reopen check still covers the earlier 58-pass checkpoint only.\n\nThe sixth batch completed with 25 further passes (1 test, 9 assertions, 0 failures/errors; `target/d1-r9b-batch-6.log`), reaching 133 pass and 22 not run. The checkpoint outcomes SHA-256 was `71eb3504c89b43404cdb3e33d06ee4f9b4f8286fafa84acfd47b5cc42530dac0`; store size was 707,662,785 bytes. The independent reopen check has not yet covered this checkpoint.\n\n## Completed Jupiter static corpus rebuild, 2026-11-16\n\nThe final batch completed the 155-fixture static rebuild (1 test, 9 assertions, 0 failures/errors; `target/d1-r9b-batch-7.log`). The progress record has **155 pass, 0 refused, 0 not run**. Every pass records its fresh admission origin and six retained addresses, including input and snapshot. A separate fresh process reopened the final store, fetched all **930** recorded addresses, and checked each input and snapshot origin against its recorded admission (`target/d1-r9b-check-final.log`). This verifies retrieval and origin equality for those objects, not admission authenticity, trace completeness, or durable published retention.\n\nKeep `target/d1-r9b-outcomes.edn` (SHA-256 `bd0e7e113a2e10a80f26402443c2f18be7cc2701e7261077b7e0772c55acda39`) together with `target/d1-r9b-store/content.jing` (733,758,551 bytes). These are scratch, not an owner-approved retention location. The frozen v1 table hash remains `e435ac4072ba0a3c278fbe91918d22184b43f0a8d6c1e397c09f68dd629beb75`. The outcomes show maximum per-fixture store growth 17,887,854 bytes, elapsed 112,615 ms, sites 451, and row closure 12,193; site total 20,805. These are static observations, not declared ceilings; store growth includes shared deduplication and elapsed includes differing batch conditions.\n\n**Remaining:** no Jupiter bounds declaration is finalized. Heap sampling was not durably recorded for these batches; C-lane quantities, serialized trace sizes, per-phase times and baseline/added work are not measured. No ceiling-governed tagged run, verification-result publication, or companion corpus record exists. The verifier and provenance gaps documented in r9 remain open. Consequently this is not a verification or reliance claim. No code changes were made during this continuation; prior red-first and kondo results are as recorded above. No commit was made. Next: retain these exact scratch artifacts, measure the missing quantities on Jupiter, implement and red-test the missing bounded/verifier gates, declare finite ceilings before the tagged run, and record any exceedance as a failed run rather than raising a ceiling.\n# D1 bounds declaration — DRAFT (static per-fixture gates; prepares the r9 tagged run)\n\nCreated: 2026-11-14. Role: VM Engineer (compiler provenance), thread\n1794422563000 (D1 correspondence), round r8 deliverable 3.\n\n**Status: DRAFT ONLY — no run has been performed under these ceilings,\nand nothing here authorizes a tagged run or reliance.** This declaration\nis written AFTER the r8 static corpus run (its numbers are that run's\nmeasurements) and BEFORE any r9 tagged verification run, per the partial\nround's requirement that a finite D1 declaration precede any tagged\nrun. The r8 run itself was NOT a ceiling-governed run: it is the\nmeasurement source. The ceilings in section 3 become binding for the\nfirst run declared under them (r9's tagged run), which must re-state\nor tighten them from its own measurements.\n\nThe r8 gates are STATIC: no C lanes were run, no guest fuel consumed, no\ntraces recorded. Lane-quantity ceilings (guest instructions, trace\nrecords and capacity) are therefore NOT declared here; r9 must measure\nand declare them before its run. cc3 v2.1 historical maxima remain\nbaselines only, not D1 numbers.\n\n## 1. Pinned corpus, revision, host, and settings\n\n| Item | Pinned value |\n|---|---|\n| Worktree / branch | /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-d1, branch d1-correspondence @ 56cc5ca3 + the uncommitted r1-r8 diff |\n| Tracked diff (git diff, all of it test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj) | 33,521 B, SHA-256 55c766cb5eef958f26b3ed03cb9169022cb66869fb8734777477fd65cd89dff1 |\n| New untracked code | src/cljc/yang/correspondence_batch.clj; test yang/correspondence_batch_test.clj (all other r1-r7 files unchanged this round) |\n| Corpus (the whole workload) | test/yang/latte_oracle/kernel_gate.edn, SHA-256 8763e273e08259686477315f41956d7005981327b7965bf01e83f9cce487c3e3, 155 fixtures |\n| Frozen v1 evidence | test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_site_tables.edn, SHA-256 e435ac4072ba0a3c278fbe91918d22184b43f0a8d6c1e397c09f68dd629beb75 (unchanged since r1) |\n| Run record | collab/yang-clojure/1794422563000-engineer-d1-correspondence-r8.outcomes.edn, SHA-256 7c2f9a6a17bdd144ba67be0326dc4b6ebdb6a83a7297ab08ac82e4ef8aef943a — 155 :pass, 0 :refused, 0 :not-run, with per-fixture admission origin, storage delta, elapsed, row counts, site count, mutation-refusal stage |\n| Upstream oracle | latte-kernel 86fca0d1d054af005cb37395eae04500d45e6279 (deps.edn :test pin) |\n| Host | macOS 26.6.2 arm64, MacBookPro18,3, 17,179,869,184 B RAM |\n| JVM / Clojure | OpenJDK 17.0.18 (Homebrew, 64-Bit Server VM), Clojure 1.12.4, -Xss64m via the :test alias |\n| Driver | d1-corpus-batch! + test-d1-corpus-static-gates in test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj; per-invocation run config target/d1-corpus-run.edn |\n\n## 2. Workload and retained object set\n\nOne fixture static gate, held one fixture at a time (maximum\nsimultaneously retained fixtures: 1; each holder released before the\nnext):\n\n- the admission: a fresh recorded admission coordinate\n  [:source :program [run-scope ordinal] 0] (distinct ordinal per fixture\n  within a batch run scope; fresh scope per batch invocation);\n- the compiled input: compile-program output, stamped AST, site table,\n  reconstruction input (captured forms/call/program/options);\n- the binding: producer C1 tree + rows, stamped tree + rows,\n  correspondence map, site-to-occurrence bindings, and the independent\n  reconstructions checked against them;\n- the persisted set: the whole v1 evidence map (content-addressed,\n  written once for the corpus), the profile (once), and per fixture the\n  reconstruction input, the binding snapshot, and BOTH row closures as\n  individually addressed rows (the 128-nesting workaround);\n- the fetch side: both complete row closures re-fetched with a\n  100,000-row bound, the replayed root recompilation, and the\n  independent gate (source hash, site declarations, bindings, C1 marker\n  coverage) plus the per-fixture declaration-mutation refusal.\n\nOne durable store handle per batch invocation (cross-process reopen per\nbatch: full content-log validate-and-replay at open). The store is the\nshared accumulating measurement store; nothing else writes it.\n\n## 3. Ceilings (separate, finite, measured maxima + headroom)\n\nMeasured maxima are from the r8 run recorded in the outcomes file\n(maximum-based rule below).\n\n| Quantity | r8 measured maximum | Ceiling | Headroom / justification |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Storage, per fixture (store growth, content log) | 17,903,978 B | 24,000,000 B | +34 percent over the maximum; covers admission-scope/ordinal string growth and row-set jitter |\n| Storage, aggregate full-corpus store (155 fixtures, content log incl. lock) | 734,451,961 B | 1,000,000,000 B | +36 percent; a HEAD manifest and companion records are additional but small (declared before the run that adds them) |\n| Row-closure size, per tree (pre-stamp or stamped) | 12,193 rows | 20,000 rows | 1.64x; the fetch bound of 100,000 rows stays as the gate's own hard refusal limit |\n| Sites per fixture | 451 | 700 | +55 percent; corpus total 20,805 sites (equals the r2 independent inventory — informational cross-check) |\n| Elapsed, per fixture static gate | 136,513 ms (with per-fixture close/reopen protocol) | 300,000 ms | 2.2x; covers the slower early-protocol shape and store-replay growth |\n| Elapsed, per batch invocation (25 or fewer fixtures, one cross-process reopen) | about 12 min | 60 min | 5x; the operated hard background limit was 2 h per invocation |\n| Peak used heap | not durably recorded in r8 | NOT DECLARED | must be measured and declared by r9's own declaration before its run; cc3 v2.1 1 GiB figure is a baseline, not adopted |\n| Guest instructions / trace records | not applicable (static) | NOT DECLARED | r9 (C lanes) must declare; cc3 precedent 4,000,000 / 1,000,000 is a baseline only |\n\n## 4. Exact reproducible measurement procedure\n\nFrom the worktree root, per batch (the outcomes file is the progress\nrecord: recorded outcomes are final; an interrupted batch loses at most\nthe in-flight fixture, which re-runs under a fresh admission on resume):\n\n1. Write target/d1-corpus-run.edn with keys :D1_CORPUS_OUTCOMES\n   (collab/yang-clojure/1794422563000-engineer-d1-correspondence-r8.outcomes.edn),\n   :D1_CORPUS_STORE (target/d1-r8-corpus-store), :D1_CORPUS_BATCH 25 and\n   (first batch only) :D1_CORPUS_SPOT \"1\".\n2. Run clojure -M:test -n yang.latte-oracle-test -v\n   yang.latte-oracle-test/test-d1-corpus-static-gates — initializes the\n   outcomes file with all 155 ids on the first invocation, then records\n   the next 25-or-fewer not-yet-run fixtures atomically.\n3. Repeat step 2 until the summary reads fixture-count 155, pass 155,\n   refused 0, not-run 0.\n4. Without the run config present, the same deftest runs scratch mode\n   (3 fixtures, fresh scratch store, resumability + finality + spot-check\n   asserts) — the standing-battery form.\n\nActual r8 batch history (all against one shared store): batch 1 was\nkilled at a 10-minute background limit after 17 recorded fixtures, and\nits resume was stopped after 14 more (31 total) to remove the per-fixture\nclose/reopen (that reopen replays a growing content log: per-fixture wall\nhad reached 136 s); batches then ran with one store handle per invocation\n(cross-process reopen per batch) at 25, 25, 25, 25 and 24 fixtures — 155\ntotal. A killed batch's partial log tail is truncated at the next open\nby the store's own validate-then-truncate recovery; the re-run\nfixture's identical content dedupes, so per-fixture deltas remained\nadditive (sum of deltas = final store bytes, exactly).\n\n## 5. Pass/fail rule\n\nMaximum-based (cc3 v2 precedent): a ceiling is met only if the MAXIMUM\nobserved value is at or under it; any single sample over its ceiling is\nEXCEEDED. Medians and totals are informational. The r8 run's samples\nare recorded per fixture in the outcomes file and were not governed by\nthese ceilings (they precede this declaration).\n\n## 6. Limits of these measurements (named, not hidden)\n\nElapsed figures are warm-JVM wall clock on this host class and mix two\nreopen protocols (31 fixtures with per-fixture close/reopen, 124 with\nper-batch); storage figures are content-log bytes including dedup across\nfixtures (a per-fixture-fresh-store retention would be strictly larger);\nthe store has no HEAD manifest (a published retention artifact adds one\nplus ownership records); heap sampling existed only transiently per\nbatch and no durable heap maximum was recorded.\nCreated-GMT: 2026-11-11 13:40:00 GMT\nCreated-Local: 2026-11-11 20:40:00 +0700\nCoding-Agent: muse\nSession-ID: 7db9b5cc-3472-4c31-9657-1b41aaa76ae3\n\n# cc3 bounded run declaration v2 — NEW versioned run (astra r4 ruling (c))\n\nThis declaration is written BEFORE the v2 measurement run, per design\n§6.3 and astra's r4 exceedance ruling (c). It creates a NEW, explicitly\nversioned bounded run. It does not amend, re-scope, or relabel the\nsuperseded run (see §5).\n\n## 1. Pinned corpus, revision, host, and JVM settings\n\n| Item | Pinned value |\n|---|---|\n| Worktree / branch | `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-cc3`, branch `cc3-lowering-provenance` |\n| Base revision | `ced9f2c2bdb43ab4a416b4ab408c76eb29245764` plus the uncommitted cc3 diff (ten tracked files, +1651/−98 at r6 delivery: the eight cc3 files plus the two F7 diagnostic scripts `test/d2_wedge_min_repro.clj` / `test/d2_wedge_probe2.clj`, which the measurement script does not load; latte oracle test file further changed in r5 for F2 caller threading — behaviour-neutral for this fixture's compiled content). Exact pin: see the digest rows below and §6. |\n| Fixture (the whole corpus of this run) | `{:id :cc3-binding :call '(latte-kernel.utils/vectorn? [1 2 3] 2)}` admitted through `kernel-compile`, bound through `cc3-oracle-binding` |\n| Upstream oracle revision | latte-kernel `86fca0d1d054af005cb37395eae04500d45e6279` (pinned in `deps.edn` `:test` alias) |\n| Compiler base recorded by the evidence harness | `7dc18478` |\n| Host | Darwin 25.6.0 arm64, Apple M1 Pro, 17,179,869,184 B RAM |\n| JVM | OpenJDK 17.0.18+0 (Homebrew, 64-Bit Server VM, mixed mode) |\n| Clojure | Clojure CLI 1.12.4.1602; no explicit `-Xmx` (JVM default max heap). JVM stack: **corrected in r6 (V2)** — the v2 (r5) measured command (§4 as originally written) activated ONLY the `:f6` alias, which supplied `:extra-paths [\"test\"]` and the latte-kernel `:extra-deps` and NO `:jvm-opts`; the project `:test` alias was NOT activated, so its `-Xss64m` (`deps.edn:52`) and its test-runner main-opts were NOT in effect for the v2 run. The v2 samples therefore stand as measured under the JVM default thread stack. The v2.1 declared command (§4, r6 revision) supplies `-Xss64m` explicitly through `:f6`'s own `:jvm-opts [\"-Xss64m\"]`, and the v2.1 results in §6 were measured under exactly that declared command. `-Xss64m` is declared for parity with the `:test` stack policy and headroom, not because the v2 ceilings depended on it: the v2 samples already met every ceiling without it. |\n| Measurement script | `collab/yang-clojure/1794386683000-cc3-f6-measure.clj` (in-repo, r5 revision: maximum-based rule, compiled-inclusive holder) |\n| Measured patch pin (SHA-256) | `git diff` (ten tracked files listed in §6) = `05076f51add1a5b5285c62c6b85c7eb8875d7c2780a7b33613e46742a250887d` (computed 2026-11-11 after the final r6 code edit; reproduce with `git diff \\| shasum -a 256` in this worktree) |\n| Measurement script pin (SHA-256) | `shasum -a 256 collab/yang-clojure/1794386683000-cc3-f6-measure.clj` = `345b432dace388ce20bb463d2241c650b400b644b5194cd0ddae1a3fb42b37c8` |\n\n## 2. Retained object set and maximum simultaneous retention\n\nThe retained set for one fixture, all held simultaneously by one local\nholder (never a global Var), is:\n\n- the **compiled input**: the `kernel-compile` result (compiled AST,\n  stamped AST, site table, retained `:admission-origin`);\n- the **binding**: `cc3-oracle-binding` result (C1 tree, rows, marked\n  and eligible occurrence sets, site→key binding);\n- the **reconstruction evidence**: the binding's stamped tree/rows,\n  stamped marked/eligible sets, site correspondence map, and stamped\n  paths — i.e. everything needed to reconstruct and verify each bound\n  key from the retained compilation;\n- the lowered images: `linearize/project-rows` output plus\n  `derive/stack-image` and `derive/register-image`;\n- the provenance relation (schema-1 map over admission/root and the\n  semantic, stack, and register call-provenance) and, in the pipeline\n  variant, its durable record in a file-backed content store.\n\nTwo holder variants are measured: **binding-only** (binding, lowered\nimages, relation, reconstruction evidence — the compiled input is\nreleased after binding) and **compiled-inclusive** (the same set plus\nthe retained compiled input). The compiled-inclusive variant is the\nacceptance variant; the binding-only variant is reported for\ncomparison and is NOT the acceptance holder.\n\n**Maximum simultaneously retained fixtures: 1.** Every retained and\npeak measurement holds exactly one fixture's retained set at a time;\nthe previous holder is released (and GC-pinned) before the next\nrepetition builds a new one.\n\n## 3. Ceilings (separate, finite, pilot-justified)\n\nPilot measurements (superseded run, r4, warm JVM, same host/JVM):\nbinding-only retained samples 7,960,192 / 7,921,728 / 8,044,024 B\n(median 7,960,192 B, **maximum 8,044,024 B**); compiled-inclusive\nsamples 9,008,912 / 8,939,024 / 8,826,416 B (median 8,939,024 B,\n**maximum 9,008,912 B**); serialized rows 293,924 B; serialized\nrelation 802,260 B; peak used heap 292,720,240 B (GC-pinned baseline\n38,967,336 B); pipeline elapsed 1,727 ms.\n\n| Ceiling | v2 bound | Justification / headroom over pilot |\n|---|---|---|\n| Storage, per artifact (serialized canonical bytes) | **2,000,000 B** | Kept from r2. Pilot rows 293,924 B (6.8× headroom), relation 802,260 B (2.5× headroom). |\n| Storage, aggregate retained serialized set (rows + relation + durable record, 1 fixture) | **4,000,000 B** | Pilot rows+relation = 1,096,184 B; the durable record is a small map over the same data. 4,000,000 B is ≥3.6× the pilot partial sum, leaving room for the record while staying finite. |\n| Retained memory, aggregate (1 fixture, compiled-inclusive holder) | **12,000,000 B** | Set ABOVE the pilot compiled-inclusive **maximum** 9,008,912 B by 2,991,088 B (**+33.2% headroom**; +34.2% over the 8,939,024 B median; +49.2% over the binding-only maximum 8,044,024 B). Pilot repetition spread was ~2% (8,826,416–9,008,912 B), so 33% covers GC-delta noise, the longer r5 run-scope strings (tens of bytes), and host jitter on this machine class, without being an order-of-magnitude loosening. The floor is the measured maximum, per ruling (c): a ceiling at or below 9,008,912 B would declare a run already known to exceed it. |\n| Peak heap (absolute used heap during the pipeline) | **1,073,741,824 B (1 GiB)** | Kept from r2. Pilot peak 292,720,240 B is 27.3% of this ceiling (3.67× headroom); the figure is absolute used heap (baseline + harness + transients), so the margin absorbs sampler/baseline variance. |\n| Time, per pipeline repetition (compile → persistence → both tagged lanes) | **10,000 ms** | Kept from r2. Pilot 1,727 ms gives 5.8× headroom; warm-JVM figure, cold-JVM limits are stated in §4. |\n| Guest instructions / trace records per C lane | **4,000,000 / 1,000,000** | Restated from the r1 record, NOT raised. |\n\n## 4. Exact reproducible measurement procedure\n\nScript: `collab/yang-clojure/1794386683000-cc3-f6-measure.clj`\n(r5 revision). Run from the worktree root:\n\n```\nclojure -Sdeps '{:aliases {:f6 {:extra-paths [\"test\"] :jvm-opts [\"-Xss64m\"] :extra-deps {latte-kernel/latte-kernel {:git/url \"https://github.com/latte-central/latte-kernel\" :git/sha \"86fca0d1d054af005cb37395eae04500d45e6279\"}}}}}' -M:f6 collab/yang-clojure/1794386683000-cc3-f6-measure.clj\n```\n\n(Settings actually in effect, r6-corrected: the `:f6` alias defined\ninline by `-Sdeps` supplies everything — `:extra-paths [\"test\"]` puts\nthe oracle test namespace on the classpath, `:jvm-opts [\"-Xss64m\"]`\nsets the thread stack (added in the r6 revision of this command; the\nv2 run used the same command WITHOUT `:jvm-opts`, i.e. the JVM\ndefault stack — see §1), and `:extra-deps` pins latte-kernel. The\nproject's `:test` alias is NOT activated: its `-Xss64m`\n(`deps.edn:52`) and test-runner main opts play no part. The\nlatte-kernel git dependency is named explicitly because the `:test`\nalias, which normally carries it, also carries the test-runner main\nopts; the git checkout is already cached locally. Verdicts are read\nfrom the script's printed `:under-ceilings-v2` map, computed by the\nmaximum rule below. The v2.1 results under this exact declared\ncommand are recorded in §6.)\n\nProcedure, in order:\n\n1. **Warmup**: build one retained structure and one full pipeline\n   pass, DISCARD both, GC-pin. Class loading / JIT are charged to the\n   warmup, not to measured repetitions.\n2. **Retained memory**: 5 repetitions per holder variant\n   (binding-only, then compiled-inclusive). Each repetition builds a\n   fresh holder held only by a local, samples GC-pinned used heap\n   (`System/gc()`, 50 ms, `System/gc()`, then\n   `Runtime.totalMemory − freeMemory`) before and after, uses\n   `System/identityHashCode` on the holder AFTER the second sample so\n   it cannot be collected early, and releases it on return. ALL 5\n   samples per variant are recorded.\n3. **Peak / pipeline**: 3 pipeline repetitions. A sampler thread\n   records used heap every 2 ms across lowering → binding /\n   projection / derives → actual serialization\n   (`dao.jing/canonical-bytes`) → durable persistence\n   (`dao.jing/materialize!` of relation and record into a file-backed\n   `yin.repl.store`, closed) → tagged execution (both C lanes must\n   reach `:completed`). Peak, per-repetition elapsed time, and\n   serialized byte counts are recorded per repetition.\n4. **Pass/fail is MAXIMUM-based** (r5 F6 fix): a ceiling is met only\n   if the MAXIMUM observed value is at or under it — retained memory:\n   max of the 5 compiled-inclusive samples ≤ 12,000,000 B (the\n   binding-only samples are reported, and also max-checked against\n   the same aggregate ceiling for information); storage: max per\n   artifact and max aggregate ≤ their ceilings; peak heap: max peak\n   over the 3 repetitions ≤ 1 GiB; time: max elapsed ≤ 10,000 ms.\n   Any single sample over its ceiling = EXCEEDED. Medians are\n   printed for information only and never establish compliance.\n\nSampling limitations (named, not hidden): retained and peak figures\nare process-wide JVM used-heap values, not an object-graph census;\n`System/gc()` is a hint the JVM honored observably here, not a\nguarantee; 2 ms peak sampling can miss sub-2 ms transients; figures\nare comparable only on this host/JVM class and only for the named\nholder scope; times are warm-JVM (the discarded warmup precedes all\nmeasured repetitions).\n\n## 5. Superseded run: failed status preserved\n\nThe r2/r4 bounded run (8,000,000 B aggregate retained ceiling,\nmedian-based accounting in its r4 record) **FAILED and remains\nfailed**. Its exceedances, restated with maximum-based accounting:\n\n- compiled-inclusive holder: samples 9,008,912 / 8,939,024 /\n  8,826,416 B — every sample over the 8,000,000 B ceiling.\n  **EXCEEDED.**\n- binding-only holder: samples 7,960,192 / 7,921,728 / 8,044,024 B —\n  the 8,044,024 B sample is over the 8,000,000 B ceiling, so under\n  the corrected maximum rule this holder is **EXCEEDED** too (its r4\n  \"under (99.5%)\" median label is corrected in r5; the samples\n  themselves are unchanged).\n\nNothing in this v2 declaration relabels that run successful, raises\nits ceiling retroactively, or shrinks its fixture. The v2 run below\nis a separate, new run under the ceilings in §3; its results are\nrecorded in the r5 findings, not back-written into the superseded\nrun's record.\n\n## 6. Exact pin and v2.1 re-measurement under the corrected declared settings (r6, V2)\n\nPin (computed 2026-11-11 after the final r6 code edit; nothing in\nthe measured patch changed afterwards — the digest was re-verified\nidentical after the diagnostic-script runs and lint):\n\n- Ten-file tracked diff (`git diff`, +1651/−98):\n  `src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc`, `src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc`,\n  `src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/derive.cljc`,\n  `src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/linearize.cljc`,\n  `test/d2_wedge_min_repro.clj`, `test/d2_wedge_probe2.clj`,\n  `test/yang/clojure_callsite_test.cljc`,\n  `test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj`,\n  `test/yin/vm/semantic/derive_test.cljc`,\n  `test/yin/vm/semantic/linearize_test.cljc`.\n  SHA-256 of `git diff` output:\n  `05076f51add1a5b5285c62c6b85c7eb8875d7c2780a7b33613e46742a250887d`.\n- Measurement script SHA-256:\n  `345b432dace388ce20bb463d2241c650b400b644b5194cd0ddae1a3fb42b37c8`.\n- This declaration and the findings are untracked collab files and\n  are not part of the `git diff` digest. Nothing is committed.\n\nV2.1 run: the §4 command exactly as now declared (with\n`:jvm-opts [\"-Xss64m\"]` supplied by `:f6`), 2026-11-11, warm JVM,\nthis host/JVM; run scope\n`cc3-f6-measure-v2-326ca2ee-2f81-4711-9377-42cd2c62e080`;\nafter-release GC-used heap 39,226,944 B; both C lanes `:completed`\nin all 3 pipeline repetitions; the run's `/tmp/cc3-f6-store-*` file\nstores were removed afterwards. All samples recorded; verdicts are\nmaximum-based (§4 rule):\n\n| Quantity | V2.1 samples (all recorded) | Maximum | Ceiling (§3) | Verdict (max rule) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Retained: compiled-inclusive holder (acceptance) | 8,828,592 / 8,832,864 / 8,888,424 / 8,829,928 / 8,924,640 B | 8,924,640 B | 12,000,000 B | PASS (74.4% of ceiling) |\n| Retained: binding-only holder (informational) | 8,203,464 / 7,920,344 / 7,918,160 / 8,014,944 / 7,923,464 B | 8,203,464 B | 12,000,000 B | under (informational; not the acceptance holder) |\n| Storage: rows canonical bytes | 312,886 B ×3 | 312,886 B | 2,000,000 B | PASS |\n| Storage: relation canonical bytes | 856,315 B ×3 | 856,315 B | 2,000,000 B | PASS |\n| Storage: durable record canonical bytes | 544 B ×3 | 544 B | — (in aggregate) | — |\n| Storage: aggregate retained set | 1,169,745 B ×3 | 1,169,745 B | 4,000,000 B | PASS |\n| Peak used heap (2 ms sampling) | 251,948,768 / 272,026,880 / 263,341,656 B | 272,026,880 B | 1,073,741,824 B | PASS |\n| Pipeline elapsed | 772 / 769 / 743 ms | 772 ms | 10,000 ms | PASS |\n\nThe script's printed `:under-ceilings-v2` map was all-true. The\nv2.1 figures sit beside the v2 (r5) figures (compiled-inclusive max\n8,931,952 B without `-Xss64m`; v2.1 max 8,924,640 B with it) — the\nceiling holds under both stack settings, which is why §1 records\n`-Xss64m` as declared parity/headroom rather than a requirement.\nSerialized sizes are unchanged from v2 (the measurement fixture's\nadmission scope is the script's own run scope in both runs).\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
