{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'd1-|tagged|trace-cap|4000000|4,000,000|cc3-oracle-binding' test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj | tail -100; sed -n '221,246p;314,327p' collab/yang-clojure/1794670000000-architect-callsite-generalization-design.gpt-6-astra.findings.md; cat target/d1-r9b-check.clj\"","aggregated_output":"2344:  \"One caller-site-tagged trace record `[fname arity caller-site]` against\n2406:  \"The ruled attribution query over `row`'s two caller-site-tagged C-lane\n2574:                              (:ast compiled) (oracle-registry yang/kind-module) lane 4000000)\n2602:                  (:ast compiled) (oracle-registry yang/kind-module) lane 4000000))))\n3235:            (str \"F2 traces the ambient-tagged context entry at its stamped site: \" lane)))\n3250:   attribution over caller-site-tagged traces.\"\n3404:     :instruction-budget-per-lane 4000000\n3405:     :instruction-budget-note \"The original uninstrumented fixtures used 1,000,000 instructions. Body-entry stream writes add guest instructions; traced fixtures have a 2,000,000 instruction bound. The harness drains only after halt. Under the D2 record lane the binding fixture's walker cell needs 2,024,912 steps (1.2% over 2M; semantic 1,105,792); the architect's 2026-11-04 ruling approves a uniform 4,000,000 acceptance budget (~1.98x headroom on the binding lane, measurement-supported, no per-fixture table). The attribution round's caller-site stamping adds one dispatcher call and one cell write per stamped guest call; every fixture in this evidence completed under the same 4,000,000 bound with the stamping active, and the trace stream bound stays stream/make 1000000 (one added field per body-entry record, no added records).\"\n3770:(defn- cc3-oracle-binding\n3888:  ;; Bounds for this tagged run are recorded in the cc3 findings'\n3890:  ;; 4,000,000 guest instructions and 1,000,000 trace records per C\n3902:          (cc3-oracle-binding compiled)\n3915:               (try (cc3-oracle-binding (dissoc compiled :admission-origin))\n3920:        (is (= binding (:binding (cc3-oracle-binding compiled)))))\n4151:               (try (cc3-oracle-binding (assoc compiled :ast duplicated))\n4192:    (let [ba (cc3-oracle-binding a)\n4193:          bb (cc3-oracle-binding b)\n4194:          ba1 (cc3-oracle-binding a1)]\n4199:      (is (= (:binding ba) (:binding (cc3-oracle-binding a)))\n4243:(deftest test-d1-live-compilation-matches-frozen-site-evidence\n4244:  ;; Static only: no instrumented machine or tagged trace is run here.\n4248:        run (fresh-admission-run :d1-static-pilot)\n4255:    (let [{:keys [origin tree rows marked eligible binding]} (cc3-oracle-binding compiled)\n4266:(deftest test-d1-amended-admission-capture\n4276:        run (fresh-admission-run :d1-amended)\n4288:(defn- d1-check-reconstruction!\n4304:        bound (cc3-oracle-binding compiled)\n4335:(deftest test-d1-capture-refusal-names-admission\n4337:        run (fresh-admission-run :d1-capture-refusal)\n4346:(deftest test-d1-amended-replay-closed-store\n4347:  ;; One static fixture only; no tagged execution and no independent verifier.\n4349:        run (fresh-admission-run :d1-replay)\n4351:        actual (cc3-oracle-binding compiled)\n4360:        dir (str \"target/test-d1-replay-\" (random-uuid))\n4363:      (is (true? (= expected (d1-check-reconstruction! (:id fixture) input expected))))\n4376:            (is (true? (= expected* (d1-check-reconstruction! (:id fixture) retained expected*))))\n4389:(deftest test-d1-independent-site-declarations-and-source-hash\n4392:        compiled (kernel-compile-in-run (fresh-admission-run :d1-independent) fixture true)\n4404:    (let [produced (:binding (cc3-oracle-binding compiled))\n4418:(defn- d1-spot-check-refusals!\n4438:(defn- d1-store-bytes\n4449:(defn- d1-heap-sampler!\n4473:(defn- d1-persist-and-check-fixture!\n4487:        producer (cc3-oracle-binding compiled)\n4543:         :spot-checks (when spot-check? (d1-spot-check-refusals! input))})\n4547:(deftest test-d1-persisted-per-fixture-static-gate\n4550:        run (fresh-admission-run :d1-r7-static)\n4551:        dir (str \"target/test-d1-r7-\" (random-uuid))]\n4553:      (let [result (d1-persist-and-check-fixture! dir run fixture)]\n4563:(deftest test-d1-persisted-another-fixture-static-gate\n4565:        run (fresh-admission-run :d1-r7-second)\n4566:        dir (str \"target/test-d1-r7-second-\" (random-uuid))]\n4568:      (let [result (d1-persist-and-check-fixture! dir run fixture)]\n4577:(defn- d1-corpus-batch!\n4586:  ([outcomes-file store-dir] (d1-corpus-batch! outcomes-file store-dir nil))\n4602:           run (fresh-admission-run :d1-r8-corpus)\n4603:           sampler (d1-heap-sampler! 5)\n4608:                                      before-bytes (d1-store-bytes store-dir)\n4612:                                    (let [checked (d1-persist-and-check-fixture!\n4619:                                                   :storage-bytes (- (d1-store-bytes store-dir) before-bytes)\n4625:                                      (println \"d1-corpus\" id :pass (:elapsed-ms outcome) \"ms\"\n4642:                                        (println \"d1-corpus\" id :refused (:stage outcome)\n4655:        :store-bytes (d1-store-bytes store-dir)\n4660:(deftest test-d1-corpus-static-gates\n4670:        run-config-file (io/file \"target/d1-corpus-run.edn\")\n4686:                          (str \"target/test-d1-corpus-\" (random-uuid) \".edn\"))\n4688:                      (str \"target/test-d1-corpus-store-\" (random-uuid)))\n4696:      (let [batch (d1-corpus-batch! outcomes-file store-dir\n4723:          (let [rest-batch (d1-corpus-batch! outcomes-file store-dir {:limit 1})]\n### 4.2 Independent reconstruction and discovery\n\nThe D1 producer is the compilation/publication composition that can retain inputs, origins and outputs. The canonical compiler and lowerer remain oblivious to attribution policy except for the side artifacts they emit. D1 is an ordinary record on a separate publication/ledger stream, discoverable by its address and its code/evidence associations. The Python site-set record is a concrete precedent for “record names manifest, manifest keeps schema” (`siteset.cljc:5-22,79-101`). The implementation must pin the actual discovery schema, signature/index projection and retention owner before acceptance; this document does not pretend the current linker automatically fetches D1.\n\nVerification proceeds in this order:\n\n1. Fetch D1, recipe, OracleEvidence and every required source/row/provenance artifact; verify their addresses and structural schemas. Reject an unsupported oracle schema before interpreting any row.\n2. Verify each code image under its own execution contract and its existing derivation chain. Report content integrity separately from code derivation.\n3. Reconstruct the source/adaptation compilation under the exact recipe, using recorded source admissions and expansion attempts; recompute final roots and eligible occurrence sets. Recompute the oracle's canonical-source-hash using its exact rule.\n4. Independently re-derive the oracle site declarations from compiled AST argument expressions. Compare with OracleEvidence verbatim under that schema's comparison rules. Do not make the producer's serialized classifications the verifier's input oracle.\n5. Reconstruct every claimed ephemeral-to-persisted binding, C1 marker set and instruction mapping. Verify exact coverage and all multiplicities, including helpers that receive no upstream credit.\n6. Execute the attribution query over separately scoped evidence/occurrence/row relations; require actual body entry in both required oracle C lanes. Reconstruct the credit set and report withdrawn witnesses and stale declarations. R7 requires re-derivation, not just re-running a query over trusted declarations (`ruling-of-record.md:48-50`).\n7. Publish a separate verification result naming D1's address, recipe/profile, verifier revision, inputs, outcomes and evidence. D1 cannot mark itself “verified”. The first additional consumer's acceptance must cite this completed result.\n\nAn implementation may share the schema decoder and canonical primitives, but a verifier must not call the producer's table derivation as its only “independent” check. The existing table generator resolves the oracle's own private derivation vars (`latte_oracle_tables.clj:15-18`); regeneration through it alone does not satisfy R7.\n\nD1 does not revise old site tables, force old module manifests to schema 2, or automatically validate the oracle's historical evidence. If actual integration requires changing a closed publication record, that specific schema revision returns to the A2 inventory. Unknown recipes refuse verification; `:trusted` is never substituted for `:verifying` (linker design `:1902-1921`).\n\n## 5. A3 adoption briefs and ordering\n\n**Scheduling:** frontend adoption starts after the in-flight cell-ref sweeps and the J2 re-run land. Refresh this inventory on that merged base before changing shared prelude/publication paths. The current sweeps, J2 and oracle continue under their existing scopes. This design does not merge, pause, or extend their tasks (signed A3/A4 at lines 21–25).\n\nEach adoption brief must cite this findings file and C1/D1 by revision. The shared occurrence finalizer/validator and provenance publication work precede or accompany frontend implementation; D1 independent verification precedes acceptance of the first frontend consumer that relies on D1. A frontend may adopt static annotation without consuming oracle attribution, but cannot call that durable correspondence acceptance.\n\n### 5.1 Mandatory host sets\n\n### 6.3 Bounds published before any tagged run\n\nThe implementation preflight record must contain actual finite numbers (no “TBD”, unlimited trace, or post-run adjustment) for:\n\n| Bound | Required derivation / failure |\n|---|---|\n| Maximum input rows, occurrences, A, D and total path bytes | Derive from the pinned static corpus; reject over-bound traversal before instrumentation. Include generated/bundled prelude expansion, not only source calls. |\n| Static side bytes and retained memory | Measure S without tracing; declare maximum per artifact/module and aggregate closure. Serialization size may be computed exactly before execution. Stop/revise on exceeding the declared storage/memory bound. |\n| Maximum records E and trace capacity C | Bound accepted trace writes for the fixture, declare C in records AND bytes including worst allowed site-id/path length, and declare drain behavior. No credit from a truncated/overflowed trace. |\n| Guest instruction ceiling and added work | Bound trace instructions per event/dispatch under each executed format, plus fixed setup/drain costs. Declare a ceiling for each host/format run before T; report baseline, absolute delta and ratio. |\n| Compile/expand/publish/verify/load/query time | Declare finite absolute time limits and allowed deltas against B/S in the preflight record. Pilot B/S measurements may set these; a tagged timeout is a failed bounded run. |\n| Peak process/heap/trace/index/continuation memory | Declare finite ceilings and measurement method; if a host lacks a heap counter, use a named process-memory measure and mark comparability limits. Missing measurement is not zero usage. |\n\nFor the oracle specifically, current code uses trace capacity **1,000,000 records**, drains after halt, and allows **4,000,000 guest instructions per C lane** (`latte_oracle_test.clj:1827,1847-1854,2453-2454`). These are the inspected baseline settings, not evidence the tagged run fits. Its own note records 2,024,912 walker and 1,105,792 semantic steps for the older binding fixture at line 2454. Restate both ceilings, the new record byte bound and the occupancy argument before T. If the implementation cannot establish enough capacity under those ceilings, publish revised bounds and their justification before running tagged evidence. Never silently raise fuel to get credit, or let a full trace stream park the fixture and misclassify it as semantic failure.\n(require '[clojure.edn :as edn] '[dao.jing :as jing] '[yin.repl.store :as file] '[yang.correspondence-batch :as batch])\n(let [p (batch/read-progress \"target/d1-r9b-outcomes.edn\")\n      entries (filter #(= :pass (:status (val %))) (:outcomes p))\n      h (file/open {:type :file :dir \"target/d1-r9b-store\"})]\n  (try\n    (doseq [[id {:keys [addresses admission-origin]}] entries]\n      (doseq [[k a] addresses]\n        (when (= ::missing (jing/get h a ::missing))\n          (throw (ex-info \"Missing retained address\" {:fixture id :key k :address a}))))\n      (let [input (jing/get h (:input addresses) ::missing)\n            snapshot (jing/get h (:snapshot addresses) ::missing)]\n        (when-not (= admission-origin (:admission-origin input) (:origin snapshot))\n          (throw (ex-info \"Origin mismatch\" {:fixture id})))))\n    (prn {:summary (batch/summary p) :reopened-addresses-checked (* 6 (count entries))})\n    (finally (file/close! h))))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '4438,4547p' test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj; sed -n '2500,2610p' test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj; head -c 3500 target/d1-r9b-outcomes.edn\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '4438,4547p' test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj; sed -n '2500,2610p' test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj; head -c 3500 target/d1-r9b-outcomes.edn\"","aggregated_output":"(defn- d1-store-bytes\n  \"Total bytes of every file currently in one durable store directory.\"\n  [dir]\n  (let [f (io/file dir)]\n    (if-not (.exists f)\n      0\n      (reduce + 0 (map (fn [x] (.length ^java.io.File x))\n                       (filter (fn [x] (.isFile ^java.io.File x))\n                               (file-seq f)))))))\n\n\n(defn- d1-heap-sampler!\n  \"Sample process used heap every interval-ms until stopped; stopping\n   answers the maximum observed. Process-wide JVM figures, a ceiling\n   measurement aid, not an object-graph census.\"\n  [interval-ms]\n  (let [running (atom true)\n        peak (atom 0)\n        sample (fn []\n                 (let [rt (Runtime/getRuntime)]\n                   (swap! peak max (- (.totalMemory rt) (.freeMemory rt)))))\n        thread (Thread. (fn []\n                          (try\n                            (while @running\n                              (sample)\n                              (Thread/sleep interval-ms))\n                            (catch Exception _ (sample)))))]\n    (.start thread)\n    {:stop! (fn []\n              (reset! running false)\n              (.join thread (long (* 5 interval-ms)))\n              (sample)\n              @peak)}))\n\n\n(defn- d1-persist-and-check-fixture!\n  \"Exercise one live admission through a temporary file store and the\n   independent static gate; with opts, also run one mutated-input check\n   per distinct gate refusal class. Does not produce a D1 record or a\n   verifier result.\"\n  [dir run fixture & [{:keys [spot-check? handle]}]]\n  (let [compiled (kernel-compile-in-run run fixture true)\n        _ (when-not (= :compiled (:status compiled))\n            (throw (ex-info \"Fixture did not compile\" {:fixture (:id fixture) :stage :compile})))\n        origin (:admission-origin compiled)\n        evidence (edn/read-string (slurp (io/resource \"yang/latte_oracle/slice9_site_tables.edn\")))\n        expected (get-in evidence [:fixtures (:id fixture)])\n        _ (when-not (and (= 1 (:version evidence)) (map? expected))\n            (throw (ex-info \"Fixture evidence missing\" {:fixture (:id fixture) :stage :evidence})))\n        producer (cc3-oracle-binding compiled)\n        independent (correspondence-verifier/reconstruct-bindings\n                      (:compiled-ast compiled) (:ast compiled) origin)\n        _ (when-not (= independent (:binding producer))\n            (throw (ex-info \"Independent binding disagreement\" {:fixture (:id fixture) :stage :bindings})))\n        snapshot {:fixture (:id fixture) :origin origin\n                  :bindings independent :metadata (:rows producer)\n                  :constructors (correspondence-verifier/context-constructors context-forms)}\n        own-store? (nil? handle)\n        handle (or handle (file-store/open {:type :file :dir dir}))\n        addresses (try (let [root (vm/materialize-tree! handle (:tree producer))\n                             stamped-root (vm/materialize-tree! handle (:stamped-tree producer))]\n                         {:evidence (correspondence/store-evidence! handle evidence)\n                          :input (jing/materialize! handle (:reconstruction-input compiled))\n                          :profile (jing/materialize! handle correspondence-text/profile)\n                          :snapshot (jing/materialize! handle (assoc snapshot :root root :stamped-root stamped-root))\n                          :root root :stamped-root stamped-root})\n                       (finally (when own-store? (file-store/close! handle))))\n        reopened (if own-store? (file-store/open {:type :file :dir dir}) handle)]\n    (try\n      (let [stored-evidence (jing/get reopened (:evidence addresses) ::missing)\n            stored-input (jing/get reopened (:input addresses) ::missing)\n            stored-snapshot (jing/get reopened (:snapshot addresses) ::missing)\n            stored-profile (jing/get reopened (:profile addresses) ::missing)\n            row (get-in stored-evidence [:fixtures (:id fixture)])\n            before-tree (correspondence-verifier/fetch-tree! reopened (:root stored-snapshot) 100000)\n            stamped-tree (correspondence-verifier/fetch-tree! reopened (:stamped-root stored-snapshot) 100000)\n            input (assoc stored-snapshot\n                         :before (vm/semantic-bytecode->ast before-tree)\n                         :stamped (vm/semantic-bytecode->ast stamped-tree)\n                         :forms (correspondence-text/read-one! (:id fixture) (:forms-edn stored-input))\n                         :call (correspondence-text/read-one! (:id fixture) (:call-edn stored-input))\n                         :source-hash (:canonical-source-hash row)\n                         :site-table (:site-table row))\n            _ (when-not (= correspondence-text/profile stored-profile)\n                (throw (ex-info \"Profile missing or changed\" {:fixture (:id fixture) :stage :profile})))\n            _ (when-not (= (:admission-origin stored-input) (:origin stored-snapshot))\n                (throw (ex-info \"Retained admission differs\" {:fixture (:id fixture) :stage :admission})))\n            replay-program (correspondence-text/read-one! (:id fixture) (:program-edn stored-input))\n            replay-options (correspondence-text/read-one! (:id fixture) (:options-edn stored-input))\n            _ (correspondence-verifier/check-replay-root!\n                (:id fixture) (yang/compile-program replay-program true replay-options) (:root stored-snapshot))\n            gate (correspondence-verifier/check-fixture! input)\n            site-id (first (keys (:site-table row)))\n            _ (when-not site-id\n                (throw (ex-info \"No declaration to mutate\" {:fixture (:id fixture) :stage :mutation})))\n            mutated (assoc-in input [:site-table site-id :arg-shapes] [:forged])\n            mutation (try (correspondence-verifier/check-fixture! mutated) nil\n                          (catch Exception e (ex-data e)))]\n        (when-not (= :site-declarations (:stage mutation))\n          (throw (ex-info \"Mutated declaration was not refused\" {:fixture (:id fixture) :stage :mutation})))\n        {:gate gate :mutation-stage (:stage mutation) :addresses addresses\n         :admission-origin (:origin stored-snapshot) :evidence-address (:evidence addresses)\n         :rows {:pre-stamp (count (:rows before-tree))\n                :stamped (count (:rows stamped-tree))}\n         :sites (count (:site-table row))\n         :spot-checks (when spot-check? (d1-spot-check-refusals! input))})\n      (finally (when own-store? (file-store/close! reopened))))))\n\n\n(deftest test-d1-persisted-per-fixture-static-gate\n   admissions through the token, and projected keys (reconstructed\n   from a single-member envelope, member index always zero) agree\n   with the recorded origin for every ordinal. Both coordinates are\n   recorded WHEN ADMITTING, before compilation, validated by the\n   same origin-shape rules as every source origin\n   (`vm/source-origin`), and retained with the compilation as\n   `:admission-origin` plain data. There is no per-JVM global\n   counter (r3 F2) and no default admission stamping every admission\n   alike (r4 F2): every caller supplies its coordinates explicitly,\n   and replay of one retained compilation reuses its recorded\n   coordinate.\"\n  ([fixture admission-scope admission-ordinal]\n   (kernel-compile fixture admission-scope admission-ordinal false))\n  ([fixture admission-scope admission-ordinal retain-input?]\n   (let [coordinate {:fixture (:id fixture) :scope admission-scope :ordinal admission-ordinal}\n         call (kernel-c-program fixture)\n         forms (kernel-closure call)\n         forms-edn (when retain-input?\n                     (correspondence-text/capture! (assoc coordinate :input :forms) forms))\n         call-edn (when retain-input?\n                    (correspondence-text/capture! (assoc coordinate :input :call) call))\n         source-hash (kernel-canonical-source-hash forms call)\n         admission-origin (vm/source-origin\n                            :program [admission-scope admission-ordinal] 0)\n         program (into (into ['(def gate-execution-trace (stream/make 1000000))]\n                             kernel-site-prelude)\n                       (concat (map kernel-trace-form forms) [call]))\n         program (into (yang/library-for program) program)\n         opts (update arg-vector-opts :native into\n                      (map (fn [[op profile]] [(clojure.core/symbol \"stream\" (name op)) profile])\n                           module/stream-profiles))\n         program-edn (when retain-input?\n                       (correspondence-text/capture! (assoc coordinate :input :program) program))\n         options-edn (when retain-input?\n                       (correspondence-text/capture! (assoc coordinate :input :options) opts))\n         compiled (yang/compile-program program true opts)\n         ;; caller-side site ids at the compiled application expressions,\n         ;; post-macroexpansion (R2), with the mechanically derived site\n         ;; table (R7); every assembled definition is instrumented\n         {stamped :ast sites :sites} (kernel-stamp-sites\n                                       compiled (into #{} (map second) forms))\n         missing (unbound-ast-symbols stamped program)]\n     (if (seq missing)\n       {:status :blocked :phase :admission :blocked-by (vec (sort missing))\n        :owners (into {} (for [s missing]\n                           [s (mapv second (filter #(some #{s} (tree-seq coll? seq %)) program))]))}\n       (cond-> {:status :compiled :ast stamped :forms forms :compiled-ast compiled\n                :admission-origin admission-origin\n                :admission-scope admission-scope\n                :admission-ordinal admission-ordinal\n                :site-table (into {} (map (juxt :site identity)) sites)\n                :site-table-hash source-hash\n                :sites sites\n                :canonical-source-hash source-hash}\n         retain-input?\n         (assoc :reconstruction-input\n                {:fixture fixture :forms forms :call call :program program\n                 :program-edn program-edn :forms-edn forms-edn :call-edn call-edn\n                 :options-edn options-edn :options opts :admission-origin admission-origin}))))))\n\n\n(defn- kernel-compile-in-run\n  \"Compile `fixture` as the next admission of `run`: the run's scope\n   with a distinct ordinal assigned by the run composition.\"\n  ([run fixture] (kernel-compile-in-run run fixture false))\n  ([run fixture retain-input?]\n   (kernel-compile fixture (:scope run) (admission-run-ordinal run) retain-input?)))\n\n\n(defn- kernel-c\n  [compiled lane]\n  (if (= :compiled (:status compiled))\n    (assoc (kernel-attempt\n             #(let [machine (compiler-test/run-guest-machine\n                              (:ast compiled) (oracle-registry yang/kind-module) lane 4000000)\n                    v (vm/value machine)\n                    ref (get-in machine [:store 'gate-execution-trace])\n                    handle (get-in machine [:resources (:id ref)])]\n                (when-not (and (vm/halted? machine) handle)\n                  (throw (ex-info \"Execution trace did not complete\" {:lane lane})))\n                {:status :completed :outcome (evidence-data v) :shape (result-shape (evidence-data v))\n                 :executed-calls (tu/drain handle)}))\n           :lane lane)\n    (assoc compiled :lane lane)))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Depth harness (max live-K per workload)\n;; =============================================================================\n;;\n;; Measurement only: no admission gate and no correctness assertions. Each\n;; kernel-gate fixture is a workload; the max continuation depth (the semantic\n;; lane's K-vector length, the walker lane's :next chain length) is recorded\n;; per lane. The same instrumentation applies to the pre-port outcome-model\n;; tree and the post-port continuation tree, so the two numbers are directly\n;; comparable.\n\n(defn- kernel-lane-depth\n  \"The max live-K depth of one compiled fixture on `lane`.\"\n  [compiled lane]\n  (when (= :compiled (:status compiled))\n    (:max-depth (compiler-test/run-guest-machine-depth\n                  (:ast compiled) (oracle-registry yang/kind-module) lane 4000000))))\n\n\n(defn kernel-gate-depths\n  \"Per-workload max live-K depth for the kernel-gate corpus, both lanes, as a\n   sorted map fixture-id -> {:walker n :semantic m}.\"\n  []\n  (let [run (fresh-admission-run :depth-harness)]\n    (into (sorted-map)\n{:scope :d1-per-fixture-static-gates, :not-a-verification-result true, :fixture-count 155, :outcomes {:minimal-last {:status :pass, :admission-origin [:source :program [\"d1-r8-corpus-4f981379-e832-4cbf-a393-e95071fe772e\" 0] 0], :addresses {:evidence :segment/blake3-e4094211c705022e962908b6176cb26b1dca6112af4345addc7acf56b21baee1, :input :segment/blake3-96565e2f01a96af55e063cc31dbc43c3a9cac7aeaf4a90888799037514286574, :profile :segment/blake3-ab1263e1c5b304bda2d1875f4fa78a7a91ca82d4c9435dffa262288e7a9863b0, :snapshot :segment/blake3-b05c02cc4651c7a9258ba510faa575c0392b393f87f496c571703b33de389b26, :root :segment/blake3-e92719a0c071f85033ea946b40cce7a8eff643b8c96116f26f75c6e96dc59b2d, :stamped-root :segment/blake3-f3bc79f03c0e152525e4f87c0666a892c579ae2b6817c48043cb92c0ee26e074}, :storage-bytes 6965459, :elapsed-ms 13815, :rows {:pre-stamp 1165, :stamped 1168}, :sites 1, :mutation-refusal :site-declarations}, :parse-bad-binding {:status :pass, :admission-origin [:source :