{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_32","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > collab/yang-clojure/1794705000000-engineer-d1-r9c-bounds-tagged-run.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md <<'EOF'\n# D1 r9c Jupiter: partial static preflight\n\nStatus: **incomplete; no bounded tagged run or verification-result publication**. Worktree mirror only; no commit or canonical promotion. The static corpus is not a verification result and does not authorize reliance. No ceiling was exceeded in a bounded run: no such run was started. The owner decision on retention location and ownership remains pending; the 733,758,551-byte scratch content store is not committed.\n\n## Pins and inherited observations\n\nHost \"'`jupiter.stigmergy.systems`, Linux x86-64, OpenJDK 21.0.13.0.3 at this continuation; HEAD `747e80fce0428f6971299819b1623b99e01f4bb0` plus existing uncommitted r9b changes. `kernel_gate.edn` SHA-256 `8763e273e08259686477315f41956d7005981327b7965bf01e83f9cce487c3e3`; frozen `slice9_site_tables.edn` SHA-256 `e435ac4072ba0a3c278fbe91918d22184b43f0a8d6c1e397c09f68dd629beb75`. `target/d1-r9b-outcomes.edn` SHA-256 `bd0e7e113a2e10a80f26402443c2f18be7cc2701e7261077b7e0772c55acda39`. Its 155 passes and 930 fetched addresses are the r9b static-gate/reopen observations, not this round'\"'s independent verification. Its recorded maxima: per-fixture content-log growth 17,887,854 bytes, elapsed 112,615 ms, tree closure 12,193 rows, sites 451, total sites 20,805. Growth is deduplicated and elapsed mixes batch conditions. These observations reconcile with the draft's proposed 24 MB per-fixture, 1 GB aggregate, 20,000 row, 700 site and 300 s static ceilings, but the draft is not a complete Jupiter declaration and those limits were not imposed on the earlier run.\n\n## Why the requested run and publications remain open\n\nDesign §4.2 requires a retrievable D1 record and recipe, image contract and derivation checks, independent reconstruction and instruction mapping, complete scoped lanes, and a separate result. The scratch outcomes retain six segment addresses per admission, not the D1 record/recipe or a pinned executable and expansion dependency closure. \"'`check-fixture!` expressly excludes admission authenticity, executable-image derivations and trace completeness; `attributed?` assumes pre-scoped complete lane traces and trusts the supplied `:complete?` flag. The runner `test/yang/clojure_test.clj` `run-guest-machine` discards the successful instruction counter, so it cannot report actual guest instructions as required. The r9 and r7 findings describe the still-missing provenance/image checks. Row-lane-only remains the stated restriction.\n\nDesign §6.3 also requires row/occurrence/path, static storage and memory, trace capacity in records and bytes with loss/drain accounting, guest work and baselines, per-phase time, and peak memory ceilings, all before the tagged run. r9b did not retain heap samples or per-phase timing, and lane/baseline measurements were not recorded. The historical cc3 4,000,000 instructions and 1,000,000 records are baseline settings, not measurements of this run, and do not establish byte capacity or completeness. A pre-run declaration cannot honestly be constructed from those missing values. No tagged lane was run, and neither `slice9_verification.edn` nor `slice9_correspondence.edn` was fabricated. Implement and red-test bounded counters, drain/loss/completeness refusal and the remaining seven-step verifier; measure appropriate preflight workloads; freeze a finite max-based declaration; only then execute and publish the actual result, including any exceedance as failure.\n\nThe two specifically named architect ruling files were not present in this worktree under the supplied names; r5 records the numeric fidelity amendment, but that secondary account is not a substitute for the normative originals. Obtain the original rulings before asserting their full compliance.\n\n## Validation\n\nThe standing correspondence, text, verifier, batch and callsite battery passed 57 tests / 703 assertions, zero failures and errors (`target/d1-r9c-standing.log`). `clojure -M:kondo --lint` on the three existing changed code/test files reported 0 errors and 0 warnings (`target/d1-r9c-kondo.log`); the standalone `clj-kondo` executable was unavailable. No implementation files were changed in r9c, so no new gate or red-first test is claimed. The full oracle suite was not run.\nEOF'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
